## 1. Topical Fit (9/10) — Excellent

The paper directly addresses 5 of 11 workshop topics: controllable text simplification,
readability measurement, LLMs for text adaptation, evaluation of ATS systems, and educational
technology. The focus on small, deployable models for resource-constrained educational settings
is timely and would genuinely interest the READIxTSAR audience.

The only minor concern: the paper generates simplified text rather than simplifying existing
text, but the CFP explicitly includes "text generation of adapted contents" so this is in scope.

