### Revised related work structure recommendation

Given the task distinction analysis, the Related Work section should be restructured as:

**2.1 Training-Time Complexity Control**
- For ATS: TinyStories, MCTune, Agrawal & Carpuat (2023) [add]
- For RCTG: Nie et al. [already present — narrow keywords-to-sentence task], ReadCtrl [add]
- Shared limitation: complexity targets fixed at training time; no inference-time flexibility

**2.2 Decoding-Time Control through Probability Manipulation**
- DExperts, FUDGE [already present]
- Limitation: require training auxiliary models; target general attributes, not readability

**2.3 Readability-Controlled Text Generation with LLMs** [new subsection — key addition]
- Malik et al. (2024) [add] — CEFR-level generation, large models, SLMs struggle at A1
- ReadCtrl [now also fits here as a fine-tuned generation approach]
- Farajidizaji et al. (2024) [add] — zero-shot prompting for readability targets (ATS variant)
- Briefly note: BLESS (Kew et al., 2023), Barayan et al. (2025) as ATS-oriented work showing
  LLM prompting is viable for readability adaptation but in the rewriting paradigm

**2.4 Research Gap and Contributions** [already present, revise to explicitly contrast with 2.3]

This restructuring:
1. Acknowledges the text simplification literature without misrepresenting the task
2. Creates a precise home for the paper in "readability-controlled generation" literature
3. Makes Malik et al. the most important comparison point, sharpening novelty
4. Correctly positions ReadCtrl as a training-time competitor for the same task
5. Is honest about the task distinction with ATS work, which reviewers will respect

